        {
          "id": "what-people-think-vs-what-really-happens",
          "title": "What people think vs what really happens",
          "description": "❌ What many owners think:",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "\"Repair is always cheaper than replacement.\""
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "✅ Reality:"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Repair addresses only the visible failure . It does not address hidden wear on other components."
            },
            {
              "type": "list",
              "ordered": false,
              "items": [
                "Timing chain replacement - £650-£1,800 fixes the chain. But the turbo, injectors, and oil pump remain at 100k+ miles, ready to fail.",
                "Head gasket repair - £1,000-£2,500 fixes the gasket. But the bottom end has unknown bearing wear.",
                "Turbo replacement - £800-£2,500 fixes the turbo. But the engine may have suffered oil contamination during the failure."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "\"In real UK workshop practice, repair addresses only the visible failure. Replacement eliminates all variables. The 50% rule is the dominant decision logic in the UK engine industry: if repair exceeds 50% of replacement cost, replacement is better value - particularly for vehicles worth £4,000-£15,000 and kept 2+ years.\" [EM-OBSERVED]"
            },
            {
              "type": "label",
              "text": "Technical comparison"
            }
          ],
          "links": [],
          "source": {
            "sectionId": "what-people-think-vs-what-really-happens",
            "order": 2
          }
        },
