        {
          "id": "the-4-step-decision-rule",
          "title": "The 4-step decision rule",
          "description": "A rules-based logic to help you decide between repair and replacement. [EM-OBSERVED]",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Step 1: Repair cost vs replacement cost"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "If repair exceeds 50% of replacement cost, replacement is often better value. [EM-OBSERVED]"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Step 2: Vehicle value rule"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "If vehicle worth under £5,000, any repair over £800-£1,500 → consider used or scrap."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Step 3: The £4,000-£8,000 rule"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "If vehicle worth £4,000-£8,000 and keeping 2+ years → replacement for peace of mind."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Step 4: Ownership horizon"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Keeping 2+ years → replacement eliminates future failure risk."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "level": "h3",
              "id": "",
              "text": "✅ Choose REPAIR if:"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Minor and isolated failure"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Sensor failure, alternator, starter, minor gasket leak"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Vehicle value under £3,000"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Replacement cost exceeds vehicle value"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Repair cost under 50% of replacement"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "The 50% rule says repair is better value"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Selling within 12 months"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "No need to invest in long-term reliability"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Default recommendation: Repair (provided the failure is minor and the repair cost is under 50% of replacement cost)."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "level": "h3",
              "id": "",
              "text": "⚠️ Choose REPLACEMENT (Reconditioned) if:"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Major failure"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Timing chain failure with head damage, seized engine, cracked block"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Vehicle value £4,000-£15,000"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Replacement cost is justified by vehicle value"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Repair cost exceeds 50% of replacement"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "The 50% rule says replacement is better value"
